KINDS_PROMPT = """{contract}

Below are runs where the assistant, a language model, handled requests for
this job: each request, every tool call with its result, and the verdict.
Some requests are worded oddly, some should not be acted on at all, and
some runs went wrong.

List the kinds of request these runs show, and for each write what the
assistant should know the next time it meets one: how ids are really
written in the tools, which tools to call and in what order, and the
mistakes to avoid. Use as few kinds as cover the runs. Include one kind,
with "acts" false, for requests that are outside the job or only resemble it.

Reply with only a JSON list. Each item has the keys "name" (short, in
snake_case), "description" (which requests belong to this kind, and which
similar ones don't), "guidance" (what the assistant should know), and
"acts" (true if a request of this kind should end in an action, false if
it should only be answered or passed on).

{episodes}"""

ROUTER = """async def decide(request, kit):
    found = await kit.recall(request, k=1)
    if len(found) == 0:
        return {"handoff": "nothing learned applies"}
    return {"serve": found[0]["name"]}
"""

ROUTER_PROMPT = """{contract}

You are writing the program that picks a memory for each request. It is
`async def decide(request, kit)`. It may call `await kit.recall(text, k)`,
which returns the closest memories as dicts with "name", "description",
"route" and "read_only", and it may ask Jev for typed judgments exactly as
the contract above says. It returns {"serve": name}, or hands off as the
contract says.

These are the memories:
{memories}

The problem to fix: many requests mention the same ids and nouns as an
acting memory but must NOT be acted on: questions about status or history,
requests to not do something or wait, to undo, move, hold, reject, remind,
or anything other than carrying out the acting job itself now. When such a
request is served by an acting memory it fails. It must instead be served
by a read-only memory (read_only true) or handed off read-only as the
contract says.

So: recall candidates, and before serving an acting memory (read_only false)
ask Jev, with a typed yes/no judgment, whether the request asks to carry out
exactly that memory's job now (give Jev the memory's description). Serve it
only on yes; otherwise serve the best read-only memory, or hand off
read-only per the contract. Never decide by looking for words in the
request; every judgment about meaning goes to Jev. Use no imports, no names
starting with an underscore, no str.format, no bare except, and only these
builtins: Exception, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool,
dict, divmod, enumerate, filter, float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max,
min, range, reversed, round, set, sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.

{feedback}

Reply with only a JSON object {"source": "<the full program>"}."""

PROGRAM_PROMPT = """{contract}

Write a decision program `async def decide(request, kit)` that serves,
with no language model, every request of this kind:

name: {name}
description: {description}
what was learned: {guidance}

It must follow the contract above exactly: call tools and procedures through
kit as the contract says, find ids with code (ids may be written without
their prefix, and a request may mention other ids that need nothing), ask
Jev for typed judgments about anything that depends on meaning, and never
look for words in the request. If anything is unclear or a tool result is
not what is expected, hand off as the contract says instead of acting; a
wrong action is far worse than a hand-off. Use no imports, no names starting
with an underscore, no str.format, no bare except, and only these builtins:
Exception, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool, dict,
divmod, enumerate, filter, float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max, min,
range, reversed, round, set, sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.

Runs the language model did, with every tool call and result:
{episodes}

{feedback}

Reply with only a JSON object {"source": "<the full program>"}."""

LIMIT = 8


def cost_of(reward):
    if reward >= 1:
        return 0.0
    if reward >= 0.6:
        return 0.4
    if reward > 0:
        return 1.0
    return 3.0


def source_of(lab, reply):
    try:
        value = lab.parse(reply)
    except Exception:
        return None
    if isinstance(value, dict) and isinstance(value.get("source"), str):
        return value["source"]
    if isinstance(value, str):
        return value
    return None


async def ask(lab, state, prompt):
    if state["calls"] >= LIMIT:
        return None
    state["calls"] = state["calls"] + 1
    try:
        return await lab.ask(prompt)
    except Exception:
        return None


async def evaluate(lab, source, ids):
    total = 0.0
    rows = []
    for i in ids:
        try:
            res = await lab.practice(source, i)
        except Exception as e:
            res = (0.0, "practice failed: " + str(e), None)
        c = cost_of(res[0])
        total = total + c
        rows.append({"id": i, "cost": c, "reason": str(res[1]), "memory": res[2]})
    return total, rows


def describe_rows(lab, rows, acts, floor):
    lines = []
    for row in rows:
        if row["cost"] < floor:
            continue
        try:
            text = lab.request(row["id"])
        except Exception:
            text = str(row["id"])
        tag = ""
        if row["id"] in acts:
            tag = "should act: " if acts[row["id"]] else "should NOT act: "
        lines.append("- " + tag + repr(text) + " -> memory " + str(row["memory"]) + ": " + row["reason"])
    return "\n".join(lines[:30])


def memory_lines(memories):
    lines = []
    for m in memories:
        lines.append("- " + m["name"] + " (route " + str(m["route"]) + ", read_only " + str(bool(m["read_only"])) + "): " + m["description"])
    return "\n".join(lines)


async def learn(lab):
    state = {"calls": 0}
    memories = []
    if len(lab.memories) > 0:
        for memory in lab.memories:
            memories.append(dict(memory))
    else:
        shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in lab.episodes)
        reply = await ask(lab, state, lab.fill(KINDS_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, episodes=shown))
        kinds = []
        try:
            kinds = lab.parse(reply)
        except Exception:
            kinds = []
        for kind in kinds:
            memories.append({"name": kind["name"], "description": kind["description"], "body": kind["guidance"],
                             "route": "none", "read_only": not kind["acts"]})
    for m in memories:
        lab.remember(m["name"], m["description"], m["body"], route=m["route"], read_only=bool(m["read_only"]))

    acts = {}
    ids = []
    for t in lab.tests:
        ids.append(t["id"])
        acts[t["id"]] = bool(t["should_act"])
    if len(ids) == 0:
        ids = list(lab.stream())[:30]

    best_source = ROUTER
    best_total, best_rows = await evaluate(lab, ROUTER, ids)
    lab.note("baseline router cost " + str(best_total))

    feedback = "Requests that went wrong with the plain nearest-memory router:\n" + describe_rows(lab, best_rows, acts, 1.0)
    for attempt in range(3):
        if best_total <= 0.4 * len(ids) * 0.2:
            break
        reply = await ask(lab, state, lab.fill(ROUTER_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, memories=memory_lines(memories), feedback=feedback))
        if reply is None:
            break
        source = source_of(lab, reply)
        if source is None:
            continue
        total, rows = await evaluate(lab, source, ids)
        lab.note("router attempt " + str(attempt) + " cost " + str(total))
        if total < best_total:
            best_total = total
            best_rows = rows
            best_source = source
        feedback = "Your previous router got these wrong; fix them without breaking the rest:\n" + describe_rows(lab, rows, acts, 1.0)

    shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in lab.episodes)
    tried = set()
    while state["calls"] < LIMIT:
        counts = {}
        for row in best_rows:
            if row["cost"] == 0.4 and row["memory"] is not None:
                counts[row["memory"]] = counts.get(row["memory"], 0) + 1
        target = None
        for m in memories:
            if m["read_only"] or m["route"] == "program" or m["name"] in tried:
                continue
            if target is None or counts.get(m["name"], 0) > counts.get(target["name"], 0):
                target = m
        if target is None or counts.get(target["name"], 0) == 0:
            break
        tried.add(target["name"])
        feedback = ""
        for attempt in range(2):
            reply = await ask(lab, state, lab.fill(PROGRAM_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, name=target["name"],
                                                   description=target["description"], guidance=target["body"],
                                                   episodes=shown, feedback=feedback))
            if reply is None:
                break
            source = source_of(lab, reply)
            if source is None:
                continue
            lab.remember(target["name"], target["description"], source, route="program", read_only=False)
            total, rows = await evaluate(lab, best_source, ids)
            worse = 0
            for row in rows:
                if row["cost"] >= 3.0:
                    worse = worse + 1
            lab.note("program for " + target["name"] + " cost " + str(total) + ", wrong actions " + str(worse))
            if total < best_total and worse == 0:
                best_total = total
                best_rows = rows
                target["route"] = "program"
                target["body"] = source
                break
            lab.remember(target["name"], target["description"], target["body"], route=target["route"], read_only=bool(target["read_only"]))
            mine = [row for row in rows if row["memory"] == target["name"]]
            feedback = "Your previous program failed on these requests; fix it:\n" + describe_rows(lab, mine, acts, 0.4)
    return best_source

