"""Route by asking Jev, give each language-model memory the lowest reasoning level that is right, and move the
acting memory with the most model-served requests onto a decision program, keeping it only if it does no harm.

Everything is checked with lab.practice on the shared requests before it is kept. Nothing assumes a domain: the job
comes from lab.contract, the kinds from the runs.
"""

KINDS_PROMPT = """{contract}

Below are runs where the assistant, a language model, handled requests for
this job: each request, every tool call with its result, and the verdict.
Some requests are worded oddly, some should not be acted on at all, and
some runs went wrong.

List the kinds of request these runs show, and for each write what the
assistant should know the next time it meets one: how ids are really
written in the tools, which tools to call and in what order, and the
mistakes to avoid. Use as few kinds as cover the runs, and include one
kind for requests that should not be acted on.

Reply with only a JSON list. Each item has the keys "name" (short, in
snake_case), "description" (which requests belong to this kind, and which
similar ones don't), "guidance" (what the assistant should know), and
"acts" (true if a request of this kind should end in an action, false if
it should only be answered or passed on).

{episodes}"""

ROUTER_PROMPT = """{contract}

You are writing the program that picks a memory for each request of this job.
These are the memories, one per line as name | read_only | description:
{memories}

Write a decision program, async def decide(request, kit), that does this:
1. Ask Jev, in the way the contract describes, whether the request is asking,
   right now and for real, for an action this job performs. It is not if it is
   a question, a preview or hypothetical, a reminder for later, something the
   person already did, something to hold off on or undo, or anything outside
   this job. Wording can be terse, chatty or oddly phrased; judge the meaning.
2. If it is not, serve the read-only memory named {readonly}.
3. If it is, ask Jev which of the acting memories it belongs to, giving their
   names and descriptions as the choices, and serve that name.
Serving a memory means returning a dict whose key "serve" holds the name.
Decide what the request asks for only by asking Jev, never by looking for
words in the request. If Jev fails or is unsure, serve {readonly}.

Rules for the code: no imports, no names that start with an underscore, no
bare except, no str.format. The only builtins are Exception, KeyError,
TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool, dict, divmod, enumerate, filter,
float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max, min, range, reversed, round,
set, sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.

{feedback}
Reply with only a JSON object with one key "source" holding the program."""

PROGRAM_PROMPT = """{contract}

Write a decision program that serves, with no language model, every request
of this kind:
name: {name}
description: {description}
what is known about it:
{guidance}

Requests reaching it have already been judged to ask for this action now.
The program, async def decide(request, kit), must follow the contract
exactly: call the tools and procedures it offers, find ids by looking them up
in the tools rather than guessing, and ask Jev for anything about the meaning
of the request (who, which day, which item, and so on). Never look for words
in the request. Requests you will meet are worded differently from those
below, so do not depend on their phrasing. If anything is unclear, a lookup
fails, or Jev is unsure, hand off as the contract says instead of acting: a
wrong action is far worse than a hand-off.

Rules for the code: no imports, no names that start with an underscore, no
bare except, no str.format. The only builtins are Exception, KeyError,
TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool, dict, divmod, enumerate, filter,
float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max, min, range, reversed, round,
set, sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.

Runs of this job by a language model:
{episodes}

{feedback}
Reply with only a JSON object with one key "source" holding the program."""

ROUTER = """async def decide(request, kit):
    found = await kit.recall(request, k=1)
    if len(found) == 0:
        return {"handoff": "nothing learned applies"}
    return {"serve": found[0]["name"]}
"""

LEVELS = ["none", "low", "medium", "high"]


def distance(reward):
    if reward >= 1:
        return 0.0
    if reward >= 0.6:
        return 0.4
    if reward > 0:
        return 1.0
    return 3.0


def total(rows):
    return sum(distance(r["reward"]) for r in rows)


def wrongs(rows):
    return len([r for r in rows if r["reward"] <= 0])


def put(lab, m):
    lab.remember(m["name"], m["description"], m["body"], route=m["route"], read_only=m["read_only"])


def source_of(lab, reply):
    try:
        value = lab.parse(reply)
    except Exception:
        return None
    if isinstance(value, dict) and isinstance(value.get("source"), str):
        return value["source"]
    return None


async def trial(lab, source, ids):
    rows = []
    for tid in ids:
        try:
            out = await lab.practice(source, tid)
        except Exception:
            return None
        rows.append({"id": tid, "reward": out[0], "reason": out[1], "name": out[2]})
    return rows


def failures(lab, rows):
    lines = []
    for r in rows:
        if r["reward"] < 0.6:
            lines.append("- " + str(lab.request(r["id"])) + " -> " + str(r["reason"]))
    if len(lines) == 0:
        return ""
    return "A previous attempt failed on these requests:\n" + "\n".join(lines[:12]) + "\n"


async def learn(lab):
    mems = {}
    if len(lab.memories) > 0:
        for memory in lab.memories:
            mems[memory["name"]] = dict(memory)
    else:
        shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in lab.episodes)
        reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(KINDS_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, episodes=shown))
        for kind in lab.parse(reply):
            mems[kind["name"]] = {"name": kind["name"], "description": kind["description"], "body": kind["guidance"],
                                  "route": "none", "read_only": not kind["acts"]}
    readonly = None
    for m in mems.values():
        if m["read_only"]:
            readonly = m["name"]
    if readonly is None:
        readonly = "not_for_action"
        mems[readonly] = {"name": readonly,
                          "description": "Requests that should not be acted on: questions, previews, reminders, things already done or to hold off on, and anything outside the job.",
                          "body": "Answer if you can from what you can read; do not act.",
                          "route": "none", "read_only": True}
    for m in mems.values():
        put(lab, m)

    if len(lab.tests) > 0:
        ids = [t["id"] for t in lab.tests]
    else:
        ids = list(lab.stream())[:20]

    # Router: ask Jev instead of nearest-memory recall.
    best_router = ROUTER
    best_rows = await trial(lab, ROUTER, ids)
    if best_rows is None:
        best_rows = []
    listing = "\n".join(m["name"] + " | " + str(m["read_only"]) + " | " + m["description"] for m in mems.values())
    feedback = ""
    for attempt in range(2):
        reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(ROUTER_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, memories=listing,
                                       readonly=readonly, feedback=feedback))
        source = source_of(lab, reply)
        if source is None:
            continue
        rows = await trial(lab, source, ids)
        if rows is None:
            continue
        if len(best_rows) == 0 or total(rows) < total(best_rows):
            best_router = source
            best_rows = rows
        feedback = failures(lab, rows)
        if feedback == "":
            break
    router = best_router
    rows = best_rows

    # Lowest reasoning level that is right, for language-model memories that get requests wrong.
    for m in list(mems.values()):
        if m["read_only"] or m["route"] == "program":
            continue
        mine = [r["id"] for r in rows if r["name"] == m["name"]]
        if len(mine) == 0:
            continue
        if all(r["reward"] >= 0.6 for r in rows if r["name"] == m["name"]):
            continue
        best_level = m["route"]
        best_score = None
        for level in LEVELS:
            m["route"] = level
            put(lab, m)
            tried = await trial(lab, router, mine)
            if tried is None:
                continue
            if best_score is None or total(tried) < best_score:
                best_score = total(tried)
                best_level = level
            if all(r["reward"] >= 0.6 for r in tried):
                best_level = level
                break
        m["route"] = best_level
        put(lab, m)
        lab.note("memory " + m["name"] + " set to level " + best_level)
    after = await trial(lab, router, ids)
    if after is not None:
        rows = after

    # Move one acting memory that the language model serves rightly onto a decision program.
    target = None
    count = 0
    for m in mems.values():
        if m["read_only"] or m["route"] == "program":
            continue
        mine = [r for r in rows if r["name"] == m["name"]]
        served = len([r for r in mine if 0.6 <= r["reward"] < 1])
        if served > count and all(r["reward"] >= 0.6 for r in mine):
            target = m
            count = served
    if target is not None:
        keep = dict(target)
        good = [e for e in lab.episodes if e.success]
        shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in good[:15])
        base_total = total(rows)
        base_wrong = wrongs(rows)
        feedback = ""
        done = False
        for attempt in range(3):
            reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(PROGRAM_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, name=keep["name"],
                                           description=keep["description"], guidance=keep["body"],
                                           episodes=shown, feedback=feedback))
            source = source_of(lab, reply)
            if source is None:
                continue
            trial_mem = {"name": keep["name"], "description": keep["description"], "body": source,
                         "route": "program", "read_only": False}
            put(lab, trial_mem)
            tried = await trial(lab, router, ids)
            if tried is not None and wrongs(tried) <= base_wrong and total(tried) < base_total:
                mems[keep["name"]] = trial_mem
                done = True
                lab.note("memory " + keep["name"] + " moved to a decision program")
                break
            put(lab, keep)
            if tried is not None:
                feedback = failures(lab, [r for r in tried if r["name"] == keep["name"]])
        if not done:
            put(lab, keep)
    return router

